+
+## Agent form tools
+
+The sign-in and sign-up forms expose client-side tools using the
+[WebMCP Declarative API](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp/declarative-api):
+
+| Page | Tool | Required parameters |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `/signin` | `sign-in` | `username`, `password` |
+| `/signup` | `sign-up` | `username`, `password` |
+
+Tools are available when the corresponding form is on the current page in a
+WebMCP-enabled browser. For local development, Chrome exposes WebMCP through
+`chrome://flags/#enable-webmcp-testing`; production availability depends on browser
+support and WebMCP enablement. Use HTTPS for deployed pages.
+
+Both tools wait for the user to review and submit the populated form. They use the
+same requests and on-page status messages as manual submissions, and return a
+success or error message to the agent through `SubmitEvent.respondWith()`. Requests
+read the current form controls rather than potentially stale React state. Sign-up
+exposes the existing password requirements as native validation constraints.
+Browsers without WebMCP support continue to use the ordinary forms.
